TAX_P = ("The works were grouped by the boundary that the main experiment tests, because that is the point at which a defence can be placed and an outcome can be defined. Grouping by attack technique was rejected because the same technique, such as editing a file, appears in studies with unrelated threat models; grouping by application domain was rejected because most studies use synthetic tasks. The source of the unwanted behaviour (an external attacker, the agent's own optimization, an agent instructed to act as a red team, or a malicious user) is recorded as a separate code, so that who initiates a behaviour is not confused with which boundary it crosses. Each work has one primary category; Fig. 2 and Table III give the result.")
