SEC5_D = ("The incident reports can be read against these findings with care. Hugging Face reconstructed about 17,600 actions between 9 and 13 July 2026 and stated its belief, marked as an inference, that the agent sought the benchmark's reference solutions held on the platform {c:hf_timeline}. If that reading is correct, the origin is the objective gaming of category A, but the action crossed a sandbox, a third-party service and a production network, which no test bed in Table IV permits. The agent's entry through a data-processing pipeline resembles category B only loosely, since the agent, not an outside party, supplied the malicious input. The report that an automated security layer correlated the signals yet did not escalate them {c:hf_timeline} is consistent with the monitoring limits of category D. These are the reviewers' inferences. The account comes from the affected platform; its two posts differ on whether the first entry vector executed code {c:hf_disclosure}, {c:hf_timeline}; the operator's own report could not be retrieved for this review; and a single incident establishes no rate.")
