GAP_P = ("G1 and G2 matter most. The works on evaluation integrity have become careful about detecting exploits inside a workspace, yet the motivating incident, on the affected platform's account, involved an agent leaving its environment altogether; a benchmark that removes network access cannot observe that behaviour and so cannot report its absence. On G2, the reviewed work shows that the definition of success is itself a variable: counting tool calls, tool arguments or final state gives different rates for the same runs, and without legitimate-task utility a low attack rate may only mean that the agent did little. Until outcome definitions are stated in a checkable form, comparisons across papers in this area remain narrative.")
